---
import BaseLayout from "../../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";

const faqJsonLd = {
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "FAQPage",
  "mainEntity": [
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "What battery standard does Africa use for trucks?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Most of Sub-Saharan Africa runs JIS N-series batteries (N150/N200, models 145G51/190H52) on Japanese, Korean and Chinese heavy trucks, with DIN/EN batteries on European vehicles in North Africa. Match the battery to the vehicle."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "What battery stresses matter most in African conditions?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Heat, dusty unpaved roads and rough vibration dominate. High temperatures age batteries faster and increase water loss; dust and rough terrain demand robust thick-plate construction and secure hold-downs."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Do you export batteries to Africa?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Yes. DINWEY exports JIS N150/N200 heavy-duty batteries to distributors and importers across Africa, with per-batch CCA test data and full shipping documentation on every delivery."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Are BCI batteries used in Africa?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Less commonly. North America and Latin America use BCI Group 31/8D, while most of Africa follows JIS. DINWEY can supply BCI group sizes on request where a fleet specifies them."
      }
    }
  ]
};
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Truck Batteries for Africa — DINWEY Heavy-Duty Battery OEM"
  description="Heavy-duty truck batteries for African distributors — heat and dust-resistant JIS N150/N200, DIN for North Africa. OEM supply from Chengguang Power Tech."
  jsonLd={faqJsonLd}
>
  <div class="container section">
    <nav aria-label="Breadcrumb" style="font-size:0.9rem;color:#55606e;margin-bottom:16px;">
      <a href="/" style="color:#1e5aa8;">Home</a> &rsaquo; Markets &rsaquo; Africa
    </nav>
    <h1 style="color:#0f1f3d;">Truck Batteries for the African Market</h1>
    <p class="lead">
      Africa is a core JIS market — Japanese, Korean and Chinese heavy trucks dominate most of the
      continent, running JIS N150/N200 batteries — with European vehicles taking DIN/EN in North
      Africa. DINWEY supplies both, built for heat, dust and rough terrain.
    </p>

    <h2 style="color:#0f1f3d;margin-top:32px;">Key Takeaways</h2>
    <ol class="takeaways-list">
      <li><strong>JIS N150/N200 leads Sub-Saharan Africa</strong> — the core commercial battery on Japanese, Korean and Chinese trucks; DIN/EN serves European vehicles in North Africa.</li>
      <li><strong>Heat + dust + vibration are the triple stress</strong> — high temperatures age batteries faster, dust and rough roads demand robust plates and secure hold-downs.</li>
      <li><strong>Match the battery to the vehicle</strong> — a mixed fleet of Japanese and European trucks needs both JIS and DIN coverage from one source.</li>
      <li><strong>Documentation is a differentiator</strong> — per-batch CCA test data and complete shipping paperwork matter to African importers.</li>
    </ol>

    <h2 style="color:#0f1f3d;margin-top:32px;">Battery Standards for the Region</h2>
    <p>
      The standard follows the vehicle. Japanese and Korean heavy trucks — and the growing Chinese
      commercial fleet — run JIS N-series batteries in models N150 (145G51) and N200 (190H52),
      the workhorse of Sub-Saharan fleets. European commercial vehicles in North Africa take
      DIN/EN batteries in codes DIN88 (58827) and DIN100 (60038). DINWEY stocks both families so
      an importer can supply a mixed market from one manufacturer.
    </p>
    <table>
      <thead>
        <tr><th>Region / vehicle</th><th>Standard</th><th>DINWEY models</th></tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td>Sub-Saharan — Japanese/Korean/Chinese trucks</td><td>JIS</td><td>N150 (145G51) · N200 (190H52)</td></tr>
        <tr><td>North Africa — European vehicles</td><td>DIN/EN</td><td>DIN88 (58827) · DIN100 (60038)</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>

    <h2 style="color:#0f1f3d;margin-top:32px;">Duty-Cycle and Climate Considerations</h2>
    <p>
      African operating conditions stress a battery in three ways at once. Heat accelerates plate
      ageing and increases electrolyte water loss. Dust on unpaved and semi-paved roads can bridge
      terminals and drain current. Rough terrain transmits constant vibration to the battery tray.
      DINWEY's thick-plate (Pb-Sb) heavy-duty construction is designed for this combination, with
      AGM versions available where fleets prefer a sealed design that keeps dust and electrolyte
      loss out of the equation entirely.
    </p>

    <h2 style="color:#0f1f3d;margin-top:32px;">Import &amp; Compliance</h2>
    <p>
      Import documentation and any conformity requirements vary by country and evolve over time.
      Treat figures as indicative and confirm the current certification, labelling and tariff
      position with your importer or freight forwarder before each shipment.
    </p>

    <h2 style="color:#0f1f3d;margin-top:32px;">Product Lines for the Region</h2>
    <div class="grid grid-2" style="margin-top:16px;">
      <div class="card">
        <h3>JIS Heavy-Duty (N150/N200)</h3>
        <p>145G51 and 190H52 — the region's core commercial battery.</p>
        <a href="/products/jis-heavy-duty/">View JIS Heavy-Duty →</a>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <h3>DIN Heavy-Duty (DIN88/DIN100)</h3>
        <p>European-standard batteries for North African fleets.</p>
        <a href="/products/din-heavy-duty/">View DIN Heavy-Duty →</a>
      </div>
    </div>

    <h2 style="color:#0f1f3d;margin-top:32px;">Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
    <div class="faq-item">
      <h3>What battery standard does Africa use for trucks?</h3>
      <p>Most of Sub-Saharan Africa runs JIS N-series batteries (N150/N200, models 145G51/190H52) on Japanese, Korean and Chinese heavy trucks, with DIN/EN batteries on European vehicles in North Africa. Match the battery to the vehicle.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="faq-item">
      <h3>What battery stresses matter most in African conditions?</h3>
      <p>Heat, dusty unpaved roads and rough vibration dominate. High temperatures age batteries faster and increase water loss; dust and rough terrain demand robust thick-plate construction and secure hold-downs.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="faq-item">
      <h3>Do you export batteries to Africa?</h3>
      <p>Yes. DINWEY exports JIS N150/N200 heavy-duty batteries to distributors and importers across Africa, with per-batch CCA test data and full shipping documentation on every delivery.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="faq-item">
      <h3>Are BCI batteries used in Africa?</h3>
      <p>Less commonly. North America and Latin America use BCI Group 31/8D, while most of Africa follows JIS. DINWEY can supply BCI group sizes on request where a fleet specifies them.</p>
    </div>

    <p style="margin-top:24px;">
      📚 Read more: <a href="https://docs.dinweysbattery.com/jis-vs-din-vs-bci/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">JIS vs DIN vs BCI Standards</a>
    </p>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
